# Tesla Model S four-door electric liftback, 2016-2021 facelift.
#
# The 2016-21 facelift car: the smooth body-colour nose with no black cone,
# the slim full-LED headlamps, and a chrome strip running through both tail
# lamps. UK right-hand-drive sales ran from June 2014 to 2021; the 2014-16
# car with the black nose cone is not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tesla_Model_S
#
# Dimensions 4.980 x 1.960 x 1.440 m, wheelbase 2.960 m (Wikipedia infobox;
# the 2016-21 car is the short end of the quoted length range).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a near-level side photograph with about 5-8
# degrees of perspective, square to the flank. The flank is traced from it and
# the front overhang is not scaled from it.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK paint document was found. White, Black, Midnight
# Silver and Deep Blue are plain names in use on UK cars. Weights 12, 10, 10,
# 8, total 40, provisional.
#
# Speed 225 km/h. Comfort 105/340, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 105. Classes 3,4.
# Dates: intro October 2016, when the facelift reached UK roads, to 2021, when
# right-hand-drive supply ended. The 2021-onwards Palladium car has no RHD
# version and is not represented.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/tesla-model-s.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/tesla-model-s.dae. References:
# citycars/references/tesla-model-s/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the LED internals, the wheels and the badging are
# simplified. The bumper trim brings the full mesh to 5.016 m against the
# 4.980 m body length.


obj=citycar
name=TeslaModelS(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2016
intro_month=10
retire_year=2036
retire_month=6
speed=225
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=105
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=340

